    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22f6Y1Nv4WY5KWBa3A7g69G)_\n\nFollows the design note merged in #80.\n\n**Before:** themes came from Elpaca packages (modus, ef, doric, lambda, catppuccin); `sp-load-theme` disabled every theme and reset the mode line *before* asking, so quitting the prompt left the bright default theme; several modules loaded themes on their own.\n\n**After:**\n- `libraries/themes/`: `lib/` (engines on `load-path`), `active/` (the 7 themes in use: `ef-dream`, `ef-day`, `ef-melissa-light`, `lambda-light`, `lambda-light-faded`, `lambda-dark-faded`, `doric-fire`), `library/` (the other 72, one folder per package, for trying out), `sp/` (own themes, empty). README with upstream commits. No Elpaca for themes; `easy-theme-preview` stays. No LICENSE added.\n- `sp-themes`: four families in `sp-theme-families` (hard light, faded light, faded dark, hard dark). `sp-load-theme` is the single entry: grouped prompt (families first, then `library`), no confirmation (`custom-safe-themes` set in code plus `load-theme` advice, nothing for `custom.el`), applies optional `sp-theme-palette-overrides` (Ef/Modus only), then disables the previous themes only *after* the new one loaded (`sp-theme-disable-others`, nil = stack). `T` loads a family. `sp-theme-appearance-themes` / `sp-theme-load-appearance` replace the hard-coded themes in `sp-macos` and the toggle; `sp-theme-dark-p` replaces the `lambda-dark` check in `sp-dashboard`.\n- Removed: `lem-dashboard.el` and its doc, `libraries/sp-archived-configs.el` (last commit linked in `sp-helper-funct.org`), `sp-disable-all-themes`, dead Modus options (`-prompts`, `-completions`, `-org-blocks`, `-disable-other-themes`) and duplicates.\n- New `docs/architecture/modus-faces-outside-global-system.org`: Modus mechanisms and the 1,237 faces a Doric-style global face system would not cover.\n\n**Checked** (Emacs 29.3 in a 256-colour terminal): all 7 themes and all 72 library themes load, exactly one enabled after each `sp-load-theme`; family lookup and `sp-theme-dark-p` right for all 7; override applied (`ef-day` cursor); toggle switches light/dark. The three edited modules were tangled from their docs. **Not checked:** macOS appearance hook, GUI, a full startup of the whole configuration.\n\n**Decisions for review:** `ef-dream` is the only `hard-dark` theme and `doric-fire` sits in `faded-dark` (near-identical backgrounds, edit `sp-theme-families`). I read \"remove the disabling step\" as \"never disable before loading\"; set `sp-theme-disable-others` to nil to stack as literally asked, but faces then mix. The old `ADR 0011` still says `lem-dashboard`'s module stays; left as history. `sp-kill-and-archive-region` still writes to its own file in `sp-setup-dir`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_013wuoefeVHQQNwZgJptsdeH)_",
